<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="practice-antiderivatives">

  <title>Antiderivatives</title>

  <exercise xml:id="practice-antiderivatives-1">
    <title>Finding an Antiderivative</title>

    <introduction>
      <p>
        Given the function
        <m>
          f(x)=\frac{1}{x}+\sqrt{x}+3\sin(\pi x),
        </m>
        answer the following questions.
      </p>
    </introduction>

    <task>
      <statement>
        <p>
          Find the general antiderivative <m>F(x)</m> such that
          <m>F'(x)=f(x)</m>.
        </p>
      </statement>

      <solution>
        <p>
          Integrating each term separately gives
        </p>

        <md>
          <mrow>
            \int \frac{1}{x}\,dx
            &amp;= \ln|x|,
          </mrow>
          <mrow>
            \int \sqrt{x}\,dx
            &amp;= \frac{2}{3}x^{3/2},
          </mrow>
          <mrow>
            \int 3\sin(\pi x)\,dx
            &amp;= -\frac{3}{\pi}\cos(\pi x).
          </mrow>
        </md>

        <p>
          Therefore, the general antiderivative is
        </p>

        <me>
          F(x)
          =
          \ln|x|
          +
          \frac{2}{3}x^{3/2}
          -
          \frac{3}{\pi}\cos(\pi x)
          +
          C.
        </me>
      </solution>
    </task>

    <task>
      <statement>
        <p>
          Find the particular antiderivative that satisfies
          <m>F(1)=3/\pi</m>.
        </p>
      </statement>

      <solution>
        <p>
          Substituting <m>x=1</m> into the general antiderivative gives
        </p>

        <me>
          F(1)
          =
          \frac{2}{3}
          +
          \frac{3}{\pi}
          +
          C.
        </me>

        <p>
          Since <m>F(1)=3/\pi</m>, we obtain
          <m>C=-2/3</m>. Therefore,
        </p>

        <me>
          F(x)
          =
          \ln|x|
          +
          \frac{2}{3}x^{3/2}
          -
          \frac{3}{\pi}\cos(\pi x)
          -
          \frac{2}{3}.
        </me>
      </solution>
    </task>

  </exercise>

</section>